# Assistant Rules Documentation

This directory contains the refactored rules and guidelines for the AI assistant when working on the Kanaliiga Eggosystem project, following [Cursor's best practices](mdc:https:/docs.cursor.com/context/rules).

## File Structure

### [cursor-rules-location.mdc](mdc:cursor-rules-location.mdc)
- Overview of rule organization and configuration
- Explanation of rule types and glob patterns used

### [01-general-guidelines.mdc](mdc:01-general-guidelines.mdc) *(Always Applied)*
- Response format conventions
- General technical conventions
- Development environment assumptions

### [02-database-rules.mdc](mdc:02-database-rules.mdc) *(Auto-attached)*
- Database schema references
- Relationship patterns (many-to-many, PlayerStats, Player-Team relationships)
- Query patterns and JOIN strategies
- Filtering and debugging guidelines
- **Globs**: `apps/backend/src/models/**/*.ts`, `apps/backend/src/controllers/**/*.ts`, `apps/backend/migrations/**/*.ts`

### [03-ui-components.mdc](mdc:03-ui-components.mdc) *(Auto-attached)*
- Navigation patterns (AutoBreadcrumbs)
- Filtering component usage (MultiFilters)
- Table styling and mobile responsiveness
- Design system guidelines
- **Globs**: `apps/frontend/src/components/**/*.tsx`, `apps/frontend/src/app/**/*.tsx`

### [04-frontend-backend-integration.mdc](mdc:04-frontend-backend-integration.mdc) *(Auto-attached)*
- Data fetching patterns (SWR with nextFetcher)
- API structure and request forwarding
- Error handling and hook patterns
- Active season filtering
- **Globs**: `apps/frontend/src/app/api/**/*.ts`, `apps/frontend/src/hooks/**/*.ts`, `apps/frontend/src/lib/**/*.ts`

### [05-api-middleware.mdc](mdc:05-api-middleware.mdc) *(Auto-attached)*
- Query parameter parsing middleware
- Controller patterns
- Model function parameter expectations
- **Globs**: `apps/backend/src/middlewares/**/*.ts`, `apps/backend/src/routes/**/*.ts`

### [06-testing-patterns.mdc](mdc:06-testing-patterns.mdc) *(Auto-attached)*
- Test structure and organization
- Mock patterns and strategies
- Backend testing approaches
- Query and filter testing
- Error handling and performance testing
- **Globs**: `apps/backend/src/__tests__/**/*.test.ts`, `apps/frontend/src/**/*.test.ts`, `apps/frontend/src/**/*.test.tsx`

## Rule Format

All rules follow the **MDC (Markdown with Context)** format as specified in the [Cursor documentation](mdc:https:/docs.cursor.com/context/rules), with proper frontmatter metadata including:

- `description`: Clear description of what the rule covers
- `globs`: File patterns for auto-attachment (where applicable)
- `alwaysApply`: Boolean indicating if rule should always be included

## Migration from Original Structure

The original `assistant-rules.mdc` has been broken down into these focused files for better organization and maintainability. Each file now covers a specific domain of the application architecture and follows Cursor's best practices.

## Rule Types Used

- **Always Applied**: General guidelines (01-general-guidelines.mdc)
- **Auto Attached**: Domain-specific rules that activate based on file patterns
- **Manual**: Can be referenced using @ruleName when needed

## Usage

These rules:
- Are automatically applied when working on relevant files (via globs)
- Can be manually referenced using `@ruleName` syntax
- Can be generated from conversations using `/Generate Cursor Rules` command
- Should be referenced when:
  - Implementing new features
  - Refactoring existing code
  - Writing tests for new or existing functionality
  - Ensuring consistency across the codebase
  - Debugging issues related to specific domains

The numbered prefixes (01-06) indicate the logical order for reading when getting familiar with the project.
